The goal of the present work is to construct the potential for non-integer values of $n$, thus extending the solution of the emptiness problem to arbitrary values of the polytropic index. As a first step, we note that 
by using the explicit expressions 
\begin{align}
    a_m &= \frac{(-1)^m}{m!} \frac{(n+m-1)!}{(n-m-1)!}\, , \qquad
    F_{m}(\lambda) = \der^{n-1-m}_\lambda F_{n-1}(\lambda)\, , 
