The following quench protocols define the non-equilibrium time evolution we study. The initial state is the pure ferromagnetic state along direction $1$:
\begin{equation}
    \ket{\psi_0} = \bigotimes_{i=1}^{L} \ket{1}_i.
    \label{eq:quench_initstate}
\end{equation}
We distinguish four different types of quenches. The first two correspond to time evolution with a magnetic field along the direction of the initial magnetisation:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:time_evolution_h1}
        \ket{\psi(t)} = e^{-iH(h_1,g)t}\ket{\psi_0},
\end{equation}
with
